1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,587
A great email only works
if people actually see it.

2
00:00:03,587 --> 00:00:08,491
In this lesson, you'll learn the simple
habits and settings that keep your emails

3
00:00:08,491 --> 00:00:10,973
in the inbox, and out of the spam folder.

4
00:00:11,823 --> 00:00:17,454
Gmail, Outlook and Yahoo decide where your
email lands based on your reputation as

5
00:00:17,454 --> 00:00:18,072
a sender.

6
00:00:18,072 --> 00:00:23,428
Two numbers on your campaign statistics
tell you how that reputation is doing:

7
00:00:23,428 --> 00:00:25,419
bounces, and spam complaints.

8
00:00:26,269 --> 00:00:30,206
A bounce is an address that
couldn't receive your email.

9
00:00:30,206 --> 00:00:31,753
Keep bounces under 2%.

10
00:00:31,753 --> 00:00:35,339
A spam complaint is someone
clicking 'report spam'.

11
00:00:35,339 --> 00:00:38,222
Keep those under 1 in every 1,000 emails.

12
00:00:38,222 --> 00:00:40,612
This campaign is well inside both.

13
00:00:41,462 --> 00:00:45,363
The biggest single improvement
is a dedicated sending domain.

14
00:00:45,363 --> 00:00:50,288
Without one, your emails go out from a
shared domain used by many businesses.

15
00:00:50,288 --> 00:00:55,661
With your own, your emails show your name,
and your reputation belongs to you alone.

16
00:00:56,509 --> 00:01:01,399
Click Add Domain, and enter a
subdomain, like mail.bloomdental.co.uk.

17
00:01:01,399 --> 00:01:07,140
Using a subdomain keeps your marketing
email separate from your everyday mailbox,

18
00:01:07,140 --> 00:01:08,983
so it can never affect it.

19
00:01:09,837 --> 00:01:14,602
Kyntlo now gives you a few DNS records
to add where you bought your domain.

20
00:01:14,602 --> 00:01:18,478
You don't need to understand
them, just copy each one across.

21
00:01:18,478 --> 00:01:21,655
SPF and DKIM prove the
email really came from you,

22
00:01:21,655 --> 00:01:25,213
and DMARC tells inbox providers
what to do if it didn't.

23
00:01:26,063 --> 00:01:29,297
Once the records are in,
come back and click Verify.

24
00:01:29,297 --> 00:01:33,961
Changes can take a few hours to spread,
so if it isn't green straight away,

25
00:01:33,961 --> 00:01:34,956
try again later.

26
00:01:34,956 --> 00:01:38,999
When it says verified, every
campaign sends from your own domain.

27
00:01:39,848 --> 00:01:42,074
Next, turn on email verification.

28
00:01:42,074 --> 00:01:47,336
Kyntlo checks each new address before
you send, and rechecks it every 90 days.

29
00:01:47,336 --> 00:01:52,126
Addresses that fail are skipped, so
you stop bouncing off dead inboxes.

30
00:01:52,126 --> 00:01:54,690
Each check costs a fraction of a cent.

31
00:01:55,539 --> 00:01:59,187
A brand-new domain has no
reputation yet, so warm it up.

32
00:01:59,187 --> 00:02:02,834
For your first sends, choose
your most engaged contacts,

33
00:02:02,834 --> 00:02:04,853
like recent and loyal patients.

34
00:02:04,853 --> 00:02:10,325
People who know you open your emails, and
that teaches inbox providers to trust you.

35
00:02:11,174 --> 00:02:12,929
Then use Send in batches.

36
00:02:12,929 --> 00:02:16,369
Set a small batch, like
100, repeating every day.

37
00:02:16,369 --> 00:02:21,072
Over 2–4 weeks, increase the batch
size as your opens stay healthy.

38
00:02:21,072 --> 00:02:22,897
Slow and steady wins here.

39
00:02:23,748 --> 00:02:25,387
Your content matters too.

40
00:02:25,387 --> 00:02:28,074
Keep the unsubscribe link in your footer.

41
00:02:28,074 --> 00:02:31,810
It's required, and it's far
better than a spam complaint.

42
00:02:31,810 --> 00:02:35,218
Avoid shouty capitals and
lots of exclamation marks,

43
00:02:35,218 --> 00:02:37,447
and balance images with real text.

44
00:02:38,299 --> 00:02:40,451
Finally, keep your list healthy.

45
00:02:40,451 --> 00:02:44,756
After each campaign, glance at
who bounced and who unsubscribed.

46
00:02:44,756 --> 00:02:50,069
And every few months, stop emailing
contacts who haven't opened anything in six

47
00:02:50,069 --> 00:02:50,540
months.

48
00:02:50,540 --> 00:02:53,768
A smaller, engaged list
beats a big, silent one.

49
00:02:54,618 --> 00:02:55,746
Here's a pro tip.

50
00:02:55,746 --> 00:02:58,001
Never buy or borrow an email list.

51
00:02:58,001 --> 00:03:02,710
Those people never asked to hear from
you, so they bounce and complain,

52
00:03:02,710 --> 00:03:05,827
and your reputation can
take months to recover.

53
00:03:05,827 --> 00:03:08,812
Grow your list with
forms and offers instead.

54
00:03:09,663 --> 00:03:12,740
Now your emails are set
up to reach the inbox.

55
00:03:12,740 --> 00:03:17,290
Next, we'll move to text messages,
with SMS and WhatsApp broadcasts,

56
00:03:17,290 --> 00:03:19,899
and the rules that keep them compliant.

57
00:03:19,899 --> 00:03:20,835
See you there.
